      "content": "i see what you're saying with cultural awareness, but it still feels like it's prioritizing \"understanding others\" over the actual preservation of one's own culture. it feels like the \"modern\" version of virtue is just being more tolerant and inclusive. wouldn't a truly balanced list include things like national loyalty or even just the strength to defend one's own values even if they're unpopular? or is that not considered a \"virtue\" anymore?",
